# SKELETON — what never enters version control.
#
# Read this before adding a line: this repo's whole claim is "no build step, no
# dependency, no node_modules shipped". Anything ignored here is something that
# should not have been in the folder in the first place, with two deliberate
# exceptions noted at the bottom.

# --- dependencies -----------------------------------------------------------
# The extension has none. The browser test tier drives Playwright, which lives
# in ONE shared location for the whole fleet (see test/browser/README.md) and is
# never installed into a tool folder. If one of these ever appears here,
# something went wrong — the packaging allowlist will keep it out of the zip,
# but a committed dependency tree has to be purged from history, not deleted.
node_modules/
package-lock.json
.npm/
.pnpm-store/

# --- secrets ----------------------------------------------------------------
# Nothing in this family needs a credential: zero network calls, no accounts, no
# telemetry, no CI that publishes for you. The store dashboards are the only
# place you sign in, and you sign in as yourself, in a browser. So a secret in
# this folder is either a mistake or a sign the tool has stopped being one of
# these tools. These patterns are a safety net, NOT permission to keep one:
# an ignored file is still on your disk and one `git add -f` from being public.
.env
.env.*
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
secrets.json
credentials.json
*-credentials.json
publish/*.credentials
publish/upload-token*

# --- OS and editor droppings ------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
*.swp
*~
.idea/
.vscode/

# --- test and build scratch -------------------------------------------------
smoke-profile-*/
*.log
*.tmp
*.zip.tmp
coverage/
dist/
build/

# --- scratch files, by naming convention ------------------------------------
# The reference implementation shipped a release with a stray scratch file in
# the working folder. Name anything temporary with one of these and it can
# neither be committed nor packaged (the packaging never-list matches DELETE).
*DELETE-ME*
*-DELETE*
scratch/

# =============================================================================
# NOT IGNORED, ON PURPOSE — two decisions worth knowing about.
#
# 1. publish/*.zip IS TRACKED. Each release zip is a golden master: it is the
#    exact artifact a store received, and it is what publish/pack.mjs diffs the
#    next build against to catch a silently dropped file. Roughly 240 KB each,
#    most of it the 55 locale catalogues. If you decide you would rather not
#    carry them, add `publish/*.zip` here — and know that you have turned the
#    dropped-file check off, because it has nothing left to compare with.
#
# 2. _locales/ IS TRACKED, all 55 of them, generated or not. They are inputs to
#    the package, not build output; regenerating them is deterministic, but a
#    package cannot be rebuilt from a tree that does not carry them.
#
# 3. publish/store/ IS TRACKED once you generate it — the screenshots and the
#    promo tile a store actually received, exactly as it received them. They are
#    OUTPUTS (node publish/shots.mjs, node icons/make-icons.mjs --promo), so
#    regenerate them on every release rather than editing them: an asset drawn
#    by hand at v0.1 and never refreshed is a description-vs-behaviour mismatch
#    by v1.2, which is a thing the store penalises specifically. The skeleton
#    ships none; the first ones you generate are your first listing.
